"""Esplora'nın Spypaper'ı tanıması için kısa kullanım kılavuzu.

Spypaper'a yeni bir özellik eklendiğinde buraya da bir satır eklenir (README ile birlikte), böylece Esplora
"bunu nasıl yaparım?" sorularında doğru sayfayı ve düğmeyi gösterebilir. Sayfa adları {SinifAdi} yer tutucusuyla
yazılır; arayüz bunları kullanıcının panel dilindeki başlıklarla değiştirir.
"""

GUIDE = """
=== SPYPAPER GUIDE (where things are; name pages and buttons exactly as written here) ===
Home screen: server cards. Card menu: start/stop, edit, open folder, "Make a Copy" (clone a server into a new folder, world optional, ports changed automatically, logs/backups/PINs not copied), "Switch / Update Software..." (opens the Server Software window; "Try it on a copy of the server first" copies the server folder with the world but without backups, installs the new software there and starts it; only if it starts is the real server updated, otherwise the errors and the likely culprit plugin/mod are shown), "Export as Template..." (.spytemplate: server.properties without ports/seed/RCON password, plugin/mod list with Modrinth versions, plugin/mod text configs, scheduled tasks, maintenance plan, anti-cheat, RAM; NO world, player data, jars, Discord address or PINs) and "Apply Template..." (server must be stopped; Modrinth plugins are downloaded, others are listed to add by hand), delete. "New Server": software (Paper, Purpur, Folia, Vanilla, Fabric, Forge, NeoForge, Velocity proxy), version, RAM, port, world: normal (seed, type) or a template map (Skyblock, PvP arenas, OneBlock, Parkour, Hide and Seek, Lobby) or "Import from Zip/Folder" (own map).
Top bar inside a server: Start/Stop/Restart, "Update" = Server Software window (update the jar or SWITCH software, e.g. Paper -> Fabric; with "Prepare the folder for the new software" incompatible plugins/mods are moved to backups/switch-..., Paper's world_nether/world_the_end are merged back for vanilla/mod loaders; world, player data, whitelist, bans, OPs are kept; Velocity <-> server is not possible).
Side menu: language, theme, text size, "Units" (metric or feet/miles; used for walked distance and world border size), "Language Wizard" (translate Spypaper into any language: source text on top, translation below, missing/all filter, placeholder check, saved as Languages/<lang>_<COUNTRY>.json e.g. de_AT.json next to the exe (also editable in VS Code, "Open in VS Code"), new language then appears in the language list; "Translate All Missing with AI" uses the AI settings/API key; "Extract Minecraft Language File" opens Game Files with "Selected language only"), "Spypaper Remote" (remote access and tunnel providers such as Playit.gg (optional account link) and Cloudflare), "Sleep Mode" (locks the window with a PIN), "Quit Spypaper".
{DashboardPage}: status, TPS/RAM, players, quick actions; Performance card with history (1 h / 24 h / 7 days; TPS, MSPT, RAM, CPU, players; recorded every minute, kept 8 days in .spypaper/perf).
{ConsolePage}: live console, send commands; right-click a line or selection -> "Ask Esplora" explains it (an error line takes its stack trace along). {LogsPage}: log viewer with translated lines, crash reports.
{MapPage}: live map. {EsploraPage}: you. "Latest Report" button shows the newest Esplora report and can ask you to interpret it. Users can type / for commands (skills) and use the + button: add image, add text file, commands, create/manage skills (SKILL.md), tone settings.
{NotesPage}: owner notes. {PlayersPage}: players, inventories, last seen, skins; stats view shows play history (last 7/30 days playtime, sessions, most active hours, last sessions). {BotsPage}: fake players for AFK farms (Paper/Purpur: Spypaper's own bot engine inside the SpypaperMessages plugin, Install button; Fabric: Carpet). Add a bot with a name, world and X/Y/Z + facing ("Take this player's spot" copies a player's position and view), a job (just stand to keep chunks loaded, attack for mob farms, right-click, sneak) and an interval in ticks (0 = continuous, 12-20 good for a sword); "Join automatically when the server starts" brings it back after restarts. Bots are ignored by anti-cheat and maintenance kicks and left out of player counts and reports. {TeamsPage}: teams. {AdminPage}: whitelist, bans, OPs; Warn / Kick / Ban / Unban with a reason and ban duration (temporary bans are lifted automatically while Spypaper runs); every action goes to the "Record" table (filter by typing a name).
{PluginsPage}: plugins/ or mods/ folder, Modrinth search and install, "Check for updates" / "Update all", resource pack, "Spypaper Mods" (ready data/resource packs: flat health/hunger bars, death coordinates, items don't despawn).
{ModTransPage}: translate mod language files.
{ContentPage}: content without mods (data + resource pack, 1.21+): paintings, music discs (own sound or Newgrounds ID), custom tools/weapons and food with stats, effects, 3x3 recipes, HUD sprites. "Design..." opens the Texture Designer: pixel painting (pencil, eraser, bucket, eyedropper, mirror, undo), templates (sword, pickaxe, apple, disc...), View: flat item, block (16x16x16 cube) or 3D model (16x16x16 voxels, layer by layer, "Build from Texture"). New placeable blocks are NOT possible without mods; the cube/3D model is how the item looks in hand.
{VelocityPage} (only on a Velocity proxy): velocity.toml settings, linked servers and join order, "Add Spypaper Server" (sets modern forwarding in paper-global.yml and online-mode=false on the backend).
{SettingsPage}: panel settings (Java, RAM), World Border, "Build Height" card (Overworld min/max Y via a data pack; with "Also generate terrain in the depths" a bottom below -64 also moves terrain generation down for newly explored areas (bedrock at the new floor, deepslate in between, old areas stay empty below; "Remove lava in deep caves" (Paper/Purpur/Folia) installs the small SpypaperNoDeepLava plugin that turns cave lava below Y -55 into air in new chunks, keeping the 10 blocks above the floor), presets up to -2032..2032, recommended RAM: 4 GB default, 6 GB up to Y 640, 8 GB up to 1024, more for larger; "Raise RAM" button; stop the server first, takes effect after restart; changing the bottom or lowering the top can damage an existing world; after a height change "Ignoring heightmap data ... size does not match" warnings for old chunks are harmless, the game recalculates them), "Messages to Players" card (Spypaper's warnings, countdowns and kick messages in each player's own game language: on Paper/Purpur/Folia install the SpypaperMessages plugin there, it reads the player's locale and picks the text; without it warnings are translated through the shared Spypaper resource pack (turn on sharing in the Content Editor, "Rebuild Resource Pack") and kicks go in panel language + English; the Players page shows each player's game language when the plugin is installed), server.properties with explanations. {ConfigsPage}: other config files (bukkit, spigot, paper...). {FilesPage}: file browser.
{MaintenancePage}: world backups, maintenance mode, "Export as Map" (world zip without player data), "Pre-generate World" card (Chunky plugin/mod, installed from Modrinth with "Install Chunky"; dimension, center, radius or "Use world border", Start/Pause/Cancel, progress; optional auto-pause while players are online).
{TasksPage}: scheduled tasks (backups, restarts, commands, announcements, "Esplora report": summary of performance, players, record, backups and disk since the last run, saved in .spypaper/reports, sent to Discord if "Esplora reports" is on; no AI needed); automatic restart after a crash is built in. After any crash Spypaper writes "[Spypaper] Likely cause of the crash: X.jar" to the console, found by matching the stack trace packages to the jars in plugins/ and mods/. If the server is still running when Spypaper opens (e.g. Spypaper crashed or was closed from Task Manager), Spypaper reattaches: console from logs/latest.log, commands and Stop over RCON (Spypaper enables RCON with a random password on server start). Only one Spypaper can be open at a time.
{DiscordPage}: Discord webhook/bot notifications. {GuardPage}: anti-cheat. {DangerPage}: reset world, restore a backup (whole world, selected parts: Overworld/Nether/End/player data or one player, or only an area around X/Z with a radius; a safety backup is taken first), "World Cleanup" (deletes chunks where players spent less than N minutes, keeps a radius around spawn, Preview first, server must be stopped), delete server (unlock by PIN or typing the server name).
Help and bug reports: GitHub Issues of Spypaper only.
"""


def guide(names):
    """names: {"DashboardPage": "Dashboard", ...} panel dilinde. Bilinmeyen yer tutucu adıyla kalır."""
    out = GUIDE
    for k, v in names.items():
        out = out.replace("{" + k + "}", f'"{v}"')
    return out
